I don't like leaving "stashes", basically - if it's a useful item, I don't
like to leave it behind. So, if I've got, say, 40K in gold, 5 amulets, 5
artifact weapons, some spare boots and helmets and cloaks, 20 scrolls, 10
rings, the high-payoff food (lembas, candy, jelly, pancakes), 5 crucial
spellbooks, 20 wands (mostly digging, teleport, and sleep), and an
assortment of tools including a pickaxe and a blessed tinning kit, that
makes my BoH pretty darn heavy right there.

You also have to bear in mind that even at my peak of playing frenzy, I
play about 10-15 hours a *week* - so running my character up and down the
stairs constantly would use up a lot of my very limited playing time. On
top of that, a typical hiatus in gaming for me is about one or two years,
so it's easy to forget what levels I left what items on. Heck, it just
took me two days to figure out where I'd left the Bell of Opening five
years ago, last time I played.

> Why would you want to take a crystal ball with you? A few scrolls can
